# Integrated Document for Task: Manage Blog Posts

## Objective
The objective of the 'PersonalBlog' web application is to provide users with a simple platform to create, manage, and share their personal blog entries without relying on a database; all data will be stored locally in text files.

## Core Features Related to Managing Blog Posts
1. Users shall be able to view a list of their blog posts on the Main Blog Page, with options to create a new post or view existing posts.
2. Users shall be able to create a new blog post by providing a title and content on the New Post Page.
3. Users shall be able to view the full content of a selected post on the View Post Page.
4. Users shall be able to edit an existing post by modifying the title and content on the Edit Post Page.
5. Users shall be able to delete a blog post from the View Post Page.
6. Users shall be able to navigate back to the main blog page from the View Post, Edit Post, and New Post Pages using a back button.

## Data Storage
Data will be stored in local text files. Different types of data will be stored in separate `.txt` files. You should define the text file by yourself in advance. This structured data storage will facilitate easy data retrieval and management through simple file manipulations in Python, ensuring the application remains light and efficient without the need for a SQL database.

## Related Files
- `main.py`
- `templates/main_blog.html`
- `templates/new_post.html`
- `templates/view_post.html`
- `templates/edit_post.html`
- `posts.txt`
}
(End for Relatd PRD)

